.SH Default keybinds
The leader cluster maps \f[CR]K\f[R] (NORMAL) to \f[CR]:lsp_hover\f[R]
and \f[CR]gd\f[R] to \f[CR]:tag\f[R] (which \f[CR]core\f[R] ships) \[em]
wire \f[CR]gd\f[R] to \f[CR]:lsp_definition\f[R] instead in your
\f[CR]src/config.c\f[R] if you prefer LSP over ctags.
.SH Connecting
Most servers default to stdio; this plugin talks TCP.
Either run a TCP\-mode server directly:
.IP
.EX
clangd \-\-tcp\-port=12345
.EE
.PP
Or wrap a stdio server in \f[CR]socat\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
socat TCP\-LISTEN:12345,reuseaddr,fork EXEC:\[aq]pyright\-langserver \-\-stdio\[aq]
.EE
.PP
Then inside hed:
.IP
.EX
:lsp_connect 127.0.0.1 12345
:lsp_hover
.EE
.SH Hover display
Hover responses render into a centered modal window.
Press \f[CR]q\f[R] or \f[CR]<Esc>\f[R] to dismiss;
\f[CR]j\f[R]/\f[CR]k\f[R] to scroll.
.SH Architecture
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]lsp.c\f[R] / \f[CR]lsp_plugin.h\f[R] \[em] plugin entry, command
registration.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]lsp_impl.c\f[R] \[em] JSON\-RPC framing, request/response
correlation, the socket pump (drained from \f[CR]main.c\f[R] via the
weak \f[CR]lsp_fill_fdset\f[R] / \f[CR]lsp_handle_readable\f[R] hooks).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]cmd_lsp.c\f[R] \[em] the user\-facing \f[CR]:lsp_*\f[R] commands.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]lsp_hooks.c\f[R] \[em] buffer/cursor hook handlers (notify the
server of open/change/close, sync cursor position).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]json_helpers.c\f[R] + \f[CR]cjson/\f[R] \[em] JSON encode/decode
(vendored cJSON).
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
TCP only by design \[em] keeps the implementation small and lets you run
a server outside the editor process.
Stdio servers can be fronted with \f[CR]socat\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
The plugin uses weak references from the editor\[cq]s
\f[CR]select()\f[R] loop, so building hed without the plugin (e.g., a
custom \f[CR]PLUGINS_DIR\f[R]) is fine \[em] the editor compiles and
runs without the LSP fd\-pump.
